# Privacy Policy for Orbital Storm

**Effective Date: October 2, 2026**

Thank you for playing Orbital Storm.

Your privacy is important to us. This Privacy Policy explains how information may be collected and used when you use the Orbital Storm mobile application.

## 1. Information We Collect

Orbital Storm does not require you to create an account, and we do not directly collect information such as your name, email address, phone number, or other information that directly identifies you.

However, Orbital Storm uses third-party advertising services, including Google AdMob. These services may automatically collect certain information from your device in order to provide advertisements, measure their performance, prevent fraud, and maintain the advertising service.

Depending on your device, settings, location, and consent choices, this information may include:

* IP address
* Device and advertising identifiers
* General device information
* App interactions, such as app launches, taps, and ad interactions
* Diagnostic and performance information
* Approximate location derived from information such as your IP address

We do not directly receive information that identifies you personally from Google AdMob.

The game's music and sounds are included with the app. Orbital Storm does not use your device's microphone, camera, contacts or location services.

## 2. Information Stored on Your Device

Orbital Storm keeps a record of your play so that your progress, high scores, awards and settings are there the next time you play. This includes:

* The stops of the journey from the Sun to Neptune that you have cleared, which decide the planets you can start from
* Your high scores: the ten best games in each mode, each with its score, the stop it started at and the stop it reached, whether it finished the journey, and the day it was played
* The awards you have won and when each was won
* Running totals of your play that awards are won by, such as the rocks you have destroyed, the shots you have fired, the power-ups you have picked up, the games and the days you have played, and the time and distance you have flown, together with the last day you played
* Your sound volumes, your chosen mode (Easy, Normal or Hard) and your chosen touch controls

The game also has a panel for testers, hidden unless it is turned on, for changing the game's numbers while it runs. Any numbers changed there are stored on your device too. Its Share tab only copies them, for you to send yourself if you choose.

This information is stored only on your own device. It is not transmitted to us, it is not transmitted to any third party, and we have no access to it. If your device backs up its apps' data (on Android, to your Google account), it may include this information in that backup, which is kept by your device's provider, not by us.

You can erase your progress, your high scores and your awards at any time using the RESET PROGRESS control on the app's settings screen. Your sound volumes, mode and touch controls are kept until you change them. Uninstalling the app erases all of it.

## 3. Advertising

Orbital Storm is supported by advertisements provided through Google AdMob.

The app shows banner advertisements on its menu and on its awards, high scores, how-to-play and settings screens. No banner is shown while you play. When a game earns you awards, it offers an optional rewarded video advertisement at the end of the game: watching it to the end collects them. Watching a rewarded video is always your choice; declining it leaves the awards uncollected.

Depending on your location, device settings, and consent choices, advertisements may be personalized or non-personalized.

Google and its advertising partners may use device identifiers and other information to provide, measure, personalize, and improve advertising and to detect and prevent fraud.

For more information about how Google uses information from apps that use its services, please see Google's privacy information:

https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites

## 4. Internet Access

Orbital Storm is paid for by its advertisements, so it requires an internet connection to play. While your device is offline, the game shows a notice and pauses, and carries on where it was when the connection is back.

To know whether you are online, the app asks your device's operating system whether it can reach the internet. It does not send anything to us or to anyone else to find out, and it does not look at which network you are connected to.

## 5. Consent and Privacy Choices

Where required by applicable law, users may be presented with a consent message that allows them to make choices regarding the use of their information for advertising purposes.

Where such a choice has been presented, it can be revisited at any time using the PRIVACY OPTIONS control on the app's settings screen.

Users may also be able to control advertising personalization and advertising identifiers through their device privacy settings.

## 6. Children's Privacy

Orbital Storm is a general-audience game.

We do not knowingly collect personal information directly from children.

Advertising services used by the app may process information as described in this Privacy Policy. Where required, appropriate restrictions are applied to advertising and data processing.

Parents or guardians who have questions regarding their child's privacy may contact us using the email address provided below.

## 7. Data Security

We do not operate our own servers for collecting or storing users' personal information.

Information processed by third-party services such as Google AdMob is handled according to their respective privacy and security practices.

Information transmitted by the Google Mobile Ads SDK is encrypted in transit.

## 8. Third-Party Services

Orbital Storm uses third-party services that may collect or process information according to their own privacy policies.

The primary third-party service currently used by Orbital Storm is:

**Google AdMob** — advertising, including rewarded video advertising, advertising measurement, analytics related to advertising, and fraud prevention.

